1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,960
This project examines whether a transparent machine-learning system can help people identify

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:07,440
urgent email without creating unacceptable risk.

3
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:11,076
I will explain the problem, how I evaluated the model,

4
00:00:11,076 --> 00:00:15,019
what testing revealed, and why the software is ready to demonstrate even

5
00:00:15,019 --> 00:00:16,990
though the model still requires revision.

6
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:23,310
The operational need is straightforward. Urgent messages can be missed when people

7
00:00:23,310 --> 00:00:25,470
must sort a high-volume inbox manually.

8
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:30,216
The model is intended to prioritize review, not replace judgment or take

9
00:00:30,216 --> 00:00:32,780
action on email. Both error directions matter.

10
00:00:33,130 --> 00:00:36,696
A false negative can hide urgent work, while a false positive adds

11
00:00:36,696 --> 00:00:39,370
review burden and can reduce trust in the tool.

12
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:43,982
For that reason, explanations and human oversight are part of the design

13
00:00:43,982 --> 00:00:46,824
boundary. Every score remains a recommendation for review,

14
00:00:46,824 --> 00:00:48,600
not an automatic routing decision.

15
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:53,567
The source collection contains five hundred seventeen thousand,

16
00:00:53,567 --> 00:00:58,018
four hundred one Enron email records, but the modeling evidence is intentionally

17
00:00:58,018 --> 00:00:58,760
much narrower.

18
00:00:59,110 --> 00:01:02,438
I used one hundred ninety-nine manually reviewed messages:

19
00:01:02,438 --> 00:01:05,350
one hundred sixty-nine nonurgent and thirty urgent.

20
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:10,218
A fixed stratified split placed one hundred fifty-nine messages in training and

21
00:01:10,218 --> 00:01:12,100
forty in a preliminary holdout.

22
00:01:12,450 --> 00:01:16,697
Urgency-enriched sampling supplied enough positive examples for the research exercise. Therefore,

23
00:01:16,697 --> 00:01:21,330
the labeled class share is not an estimate of a normal mailbox.

24
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:26,023
The sample supports controlled experimentation, but not broad operational reliability.

25
00:01:26,023 --> 00:01:30,800
Raw message content and reviewer notes remain excluded from the repository.

26
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:35,870
Demographic fairness was not tested because protected demographic fields were unavailable.

27
00:01:37,870 --> 00:01:40,590
The project advanced through controlled checkpoints.

28
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:45,560
The Week three baseline established a reproducible T F I D F

29
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:47,100
and logistic-regression reference model.

30
00:01:47,450 --> 00:01:54,050
Week four tested twenty-four class-balanced configurations using five-fold cross-validation and added global

31
00:01:54,050 --> 00:01:56,250
and case-level SHAP explanations.

32
00:01:56,600 --> 00:02:01,021
Week six separated threshold selection from evaluation through nested cross-validation,

33
00:02:01,021 --> 00:02:05,000
then froze the decision before the preliminary holdout comparison.

34
00:02:05,350 --> 00:02:08,070
Week seven added a separate readiness framework.

35
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:13,333
Gate A tests whether the software can support a safe local demonstration.

36
00:02:13,333 --> 00:02:15,380
Gate B tests predictive reliability.

37
00:02:15,730 --> 00:02:19,690
This separation prevents a functioning interface from being treated as proof that

38
00:02:19,690 --> 00:02:21,010
the classifier is reliable.

39
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:28,050
I tested twenty-four class-balanced configurations and selected the strongest training candidate.

40
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:32,579
Its mean cross-validated urgent F one increased from six point seven percent

41
00:02:32,579 --> 00:02:34,320
to eleven point four percent.

42
00:02:34,670 --> 00:02:38,830
Urgent recall also doubled, rising from four percent to eight percent.

43
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:43,596
The feature space decreased from four thousand ninety-seven to two thousand eight

44
00:02:43,596 --> 00:02:44,700
hundred ninety-five features.

45
00:02:45,050 --> 00:02:48,037
However, the preliminary holdout result did not improve.

46
00:02:48,037 --> 00:02:51,023
Urgent F one remained forty-four point four percent,

47
00:02:51,023 --> 00:02:54,010
with four false negatives and one false positive.

48
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:58,346
The optimization made the model smaller and improved the training evidence,

49
00:02:58,346 --> 00:03:00,520
but it did not establish generalization.

50
00:03:00,870 --> 00:03:04,630
The complete selected configuration is documented in the repository.

51
00:03:06,630 --> 00:03:10,710
Week six threshold testing exposed the central reliability problem.

52
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:15,592
At zero point four five, urgent recall reached one hundred percent,

53
00:03:15,592 --> 00:03:19,300
but only because every training message was labeled urgent.

54
00:03:19,650 --> 00:03:23,712
That created one hundred thirty-five false positives and reduced triage to reviewing

55
00:03:23,712 --> 00:03:24,050
everything.

56
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:28,816
At zero point five zero, the model produced no false positives in

57
00:03:28,816 --> 00:03:29,920
the outer-fold predictions.

58
00:03:30,270 --> 00:03:33,330
However, it found only two of twenty-four urgent messages.

59
00:03:33,330 --> 00:03:37,070
Recall fell to eight point three percent, with twenty-two false negatives.

60
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:41,671
The probability scores were also highly compressed. One hundred fifty-seven of one

61
00:03:41,671 --> 00:03:45,923
hundred fifty-nine out-of-fold probabilities fell from zero point four five to below

62
00:03:45,923 --> 00:03:47,340
zero point five zero.

63
00:03:47,690 --> 00:03:51,610
A small threshold change therefore flips nearly the entire workload.

64
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:55,964
Neither operating point balances urgent-message detection with a manageable review burden.

65
00:03:55,964 --> 00:03:59,240
Changing the threshold alone does not solve the problem.

66
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:03,960
The evidence supports two different conclusions.

67
00:04:04,310 --> 00:04:08,070
First, Gate A passed. All thirteen automated tests passed.

68
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:12,740
The validator also completed sixty deterministic synthetic inference runs.

69
00:04:13,090 --> 00:04:18,999
Those runs checked visible thresholds, bounded explanations, privacy-safe output, input validation,

70
00:04:18,999 --> 00:04:20,610
and human-review status.

71
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:24,720
They also confirmed safe failure when the local model is unavailable.

72
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:29,342
Second, Gate B failed, so the model remains in the revise category.

73
00:04:29,342 --> 00:04:32,190
In practical terms, the model still needs revision.

74
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:37,134
The working Fast API demonstration shows that the research workflow can be

75
00:04:37,134 --> 00:04:37,900
demonstrated repeatably.

76
00:04:38,250 --> 00:04:43,230
It does not establish predictive reliability. It does not authorize shadow testing

77
00:04:43,230 --> 00:04:44,890
or approve production deployment.

78
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:50,340
No automated email action is permitted, and the locally generated model artifact

79
00:04:50,340 --> 00:04:52,040
remains excluded from Git.

80
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:58,200
The next work should improve the evidence, not expand deployment claims.

81
00:04:58,550 --> 00:05:02,657
Increase the reviewed sample, preserve a truly untouched final test set,

82
00:05:02,657 --> 00:05:07,137
and investigate calibration, vocabulary coverage, and the failure patterns behind both error

83
00:05:07,137 --> 00:05:07,510
types.

84
00:05:07,860 --> 00:05:12,889
Then repeat the controlled evaluation under the same privacy, reproducibility, workload,

85
00:05:12,889 --> 00:05:14,260
and human-approval gates.

86
00:05:14,610 --> 00:05:19,250
The software workflow is ready to demonstrate, while the classifier still needs

87
00:05:19,250 --> 00:05:21,570
better evidence before any operational recommendation.

88
00:05:23,570 --> 00:05:26,370
The project repository is shown on this slide.

89
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:31,459
It contains the code, executed notebooks, test results, decision records,

90
00:05:31,459 --> 00:05:32,880
and reproducibility guidance.

91
00:05:33,230 --> 00:05:36,030
I can be reached at the university email shown. Thank you.
